<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaSkittish.xml                           Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  WHY
  ===
  BTD_Jawa carried Turn_Gene_Terrified (Integrated Genes, load 180), which fires
  Turn_MentalBreak_TerrifiedFaintingSpell — the carrier simply collapses mid-
  firefight. Observed in-game 2026-08-11: a Jawa fainted during the ion blaster
  test. Perfect flavour, unplayable when every colonist is a Jawa.

  Turn_Gene_Terrified is used by exactly four xenotypes in the active load set:

      guy762_xenotype_jawa        guy762_xenotype_nemoidian
      BTD_Jawa                    BTD_Neimoidian

  Jawa and Neimoidians — both canonically cowardly, and Neimoidians are NPCs
  only. So rather than soften a shared gene and flatten the Trade Federation
  along with us, this authors a Jawa-only replacement and leaves the original
  untouched for everyone else. NPC Neimoidians keep fainting, which is a joy.

  WHAT CHANGED FROM THE DONOR
  ===========================
  Cloned from Turn_Gene_Terrified with two deletions and one reduction:

      geneClass       IntegratedGenes.Gene_Terrified  -> REMOVED  (no C# behaviour)
      mentalBreakDef  ..TerrifiedFaintingSpell        -> REMOVED  (no collapsing)
      biostatMet      +2                              -> +1

  Kept: Terror x1.5. That is the part worth keeping — Jawa are still unusually
  sensitive to terror, they are still poor soldiers on paper, and the campaign's
  "win by patience, numbers and good ground" doctrine still holds. They simply
  stay conscious while doing it.

  The metabolism drops from +2 to +1 deliberately. In Biotech's economy a
  drawback pays the xenotype, and removing the fainting removes most of the
  drawback. Claiming the full +2 for a gene that now only multiplies Terror
  would be quietly buying a free point of metabolism. If BTD_Jawa's totals need
  rebalancing after this, that belongs in jawa_xenotype_and_religion.md, not
  here.

  ⚠️ NOT a drop-in stat match for the donor. RoyalFavorValue +0.5 is also gone,
  since it was compensation for the fainting. Nobody in this campaign is farming
  royal favour with Jawa, but say it out loud rather than let it be discovered.

  IF THE FAINTING IS EVER WANTED BACK
  ===================================
  The right home is a second, NPC-only Jawa xenotype carrying the original gene,
  built the way GamorreanXenotype.xml was, with wild/raider Jawa pawnkinds
  pointed at it. Then the player's Jawa stay upright and everyone else's faint.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GeneDef>
    <defName>Jawa_Gene_Skittish</defName>
    <label>skittish</label>
    <labelShortAdj>skittish</labelShortAdj>
    <description>Carriers of this gene have an overactive fight-or-flight response. Loud noises, blood and violence rattle them badly, and they feel dread far more keenly than others do — but they stay on their feet. A skittish Jawa does not stand and trade fire; it finds cover, finds numbers, and finds a better angle.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_Terrified</iconPath>
    <displayCategory>Turn_GeneCategory_Slavery</displayCategory>
    <displayOrderInCategory>1780</displayOrderInCategory>
    <biostatMet>1</biostatMet>
    <statFactors>
      <Terror>1.5</Terror>
    </statFactors>
  </GeneDef>

</Defs>
